John Gregory wrote:

 > I'm officially too old to play NetHack.

Hey, I'm 65, and by no means the oldest poster here.
Don't give up on NetHack until you are looking at
the daisies from the root end.

 > Today I lost a viable character to a floating eye
 > for the umpteenth time.

In NetHack, instead of "haste makes waste" it's
either "haste makes tombstones" or "haste makes
log file entries".

 > I hate the blue color, I can not see it on the
 > black background,

It is really a shame that the current color
selections are limited to those of a long superseded
display technology. I've got 2^24 colors available,
and I'm sure so do most NetHack players by now. Some
way to do a better mapping of the NetHack colors to
display colors would certainly be a nice patch for
someone to create. The existing palette of NetHack
colors is small enough in number that they could all
be assigned RGB values in a nethack.rc / defaults.nh
file OPTIONS clause without bulking up that file
tremendously.

 > I have fiddled with the brightness and contrast
 > control on my monitor, and I don't know how to
 > make the situation better.

The problem is discussed here often, and there may
be some solutions offered in the NetHack wiki by
now.

Alternatively, it may be time to join the rest of us
old blind coots and shift to a tiles version just so
you can see the monsters. There are some truly
enormous tile sets available if you have a monitor
with sufficient pixel dimensions to make them
useful. I happen to prefer the 20x40 tile set Robert
M. Cook (the web comic artist who writes and draws
_The Mansion of E_) offers, just because it fits
usual screen aspect ratios well.

http://www.olywa.net/cook/nhack.htm

